test:ci excludes all 8 mirror-covered suites with tests:
  @tealstreet/tealchart (tealchart)
  @tealstreet/tealscript (tealchart)
  @tealstreet/cli-core (tealstreet-sdk)
  @tealstreet/oems-core (tealstreet-sdk)
  @tealstreet/safe-cex (tealstreet-sdk)
  @tealstreet/script-api-web (tealstreet-sdk)
  @tealstreet/service-telemetry (tealstreet-sdk)
  @tealstreet/cli (tealstreet-sdk)
Also excluded for non-mirror reasons: tealstreet-next
Kept on self-hosted despite the mirror: @tealstreet/script-authoring — script-types-bundle.test.ts is describe.skipIf(generator === null) on the repo root's scripts/ directory, which the slice does not ship, so on the mirror it SKIPS. The drift it guards is caught instead by ci.yaml's "Check script types have not drifted" step — do not delete that step believing the mirror covers it.
Kept on self-hosted despite the mirror: @tealstreet/script-api-core — orderEntryPoints.test.ts and noHandRolledAdapters.test.ts are it.skipIf(!HAS_WEB_APP) — they grep apps/web, which the tealstreet-sdk slice does not ship, so on the mirror they SKIP. Root CLAUDE.md holds the order-entry-point registry up as the model for a load-bearing guard, so it keeps running on self-hosted.
